The person who signed the decree suspending the Communist Party of the Russian SFSR is Yeltsin, as stated in passage {"idx": 12572, "paragraph_text": "On August 23, after the failure of GKChP, in the presence of Gorbachev, Yeltsin signed a decree suspending all activity by the Communist Party of the Russian SFSR in the territory of Russia."}

The bilateral pact signed by Kravchuk and Yeltsin lasted 10 years, as stated in passage {"idx": 12569, "paragraph_text": "On November 19, the chairmen of the Ukrainian and Russian parliaments, respectively, Kravchuk and Yeltsin, signed a 10-year bilateral pact."}

Therefore, the pact between Kravchuk and the person who signed the decree suspending the Communist Party of the Russian SFSR (Yeltsin) lasted 10 years.

FINAL_ANSWER: 10 years
